  "correction_rules": [
    "Near-term (days 1–15) shows a consistent low bias: true outcomes are typically ~+0.2 to +1.5 EUR above the model, especially during rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift to the first half of the path.",
    "The model overstates persistence of late-horizon drawdowns (days ~20–30): forecasts drift too low vs realized, which often stabilizes or rebounds. Damp negative trends beyond ~3 weeks and pull forecasts back toward the recent mean.",
    "After upside spikes, the model underestimates the follow-through (it mean-reverts too quickly). When the last 5–10 days show a strong upswing, reduce mean-reversion strength and allow a higher plateau for ~1–2 weeks.",
    "Peak/trough amplitude is slightly muted: highs are under-forecast and subsequent declines are over-forecast. Apply a mild convex adjustment—boost forecasts when momentum is positive; soften declines when momentum is negative.",
    "Horizon-dependent calibration: use larger bias correction early (week 1–2) and stronger mean-reversion/variance dampening later (week 3–4), rather than a single uniform adjustment."
  ]
